title REDS %788 measured -- the population of scripts that cannot find their root in a bare checkout
prompt fleet lap; the card's agent-doable queue stood claimed by peers, so reds first took the OPEN row in my own lane
rota lap 5219, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the concrete fact at the door was a directory name, and the whole lap follows from git ls-files rishi/bin reading 0
think %788 gives its sweep to the fleet -- one word in files spread across every lane -- so a ship may not sweep. What a ship may land is the reading the sweep will be timed against.
think Nothing in this tree could see the population. Every standing guard runs in a tree somebody has already built in, which is the one condition that hides the fault, and control_perturbation reaches the class only by running a candidate twice in a detached worktree at two to three minutes each.
think tools/fixtures/r/root_finder_scan.sh extracts, from each tracked shell source, the sentinel directory names its walking loop tests, and asks git ls-files whether each name holds tracked content. Static, no build, no worktree.
think Three classes rather than one: tracked, build_output, and git_dir. A .git sentinel runs in a clone and refuses in a linked worktree, where git worktree add writes .git as a FILE -- a narrower fault wanting a different repair, so it is counted apart.
think A walking loop is told from a wait loop by the dirname reassignment of the very variable the test names. The first draft read a run-lock wait loop as a root-finder and invented a build-output sentinel from it.
obs 214 finders read, 189 bare_unrunnable, 9 worktree_fragile, 0 ambiguous, over 3,723 tracked shell sources. The ceiling is 189 with no slack, and it ratchets rather than walls because a wall at zero would red eight ships at once for a sweep none of them chose this hour.
obs The scan and its control name rishi/src and tools/fixtures, both tracked, so they stand in finders and never in the gated number -- proven by a leg reading the scan's own --explain rather than by the sentence saying so.
obs One mutation taught its own lesson. A guard spelled as assign a sentinel, then test it is two halves; removing the test alone bit nothing, because the poisoned value still refused downstream. The mutation had to remove the ASSIGNMENT.
obs A second door nobody has weighed: one tracked file under rishi/bin would fix all 189 with two files touched rather than 189, at the cost of a build-output room holding tracked content. Named on the card rather than taken.
obs Reds first found a second on the way. fold_shelf_link_repoint read fold_depth_lost=5 -- two of them my own new shelf, three standing from peers' shelves landed earlier tonight. The repointer applied all five; every one is a proven depth correction to a link that already resolves.
obs The prevention lives one directory over and I missed it: tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold_reanchor.sh rewrites a block's links AT WRITE TIME for exactly the construction-to-archive move a landed-accounts shelf makes.
loom witness=root_finder scan_ms=9300 control_ms=15200 sources=3723 finders=214
